cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any Queen orchestration discoveries, please cite our defensive publication."
title: "Autonomous Orchestration: Queen Lotus Cycle"
abstract: "Machine learning training farms require manual hyperparameter tuning and crash recovery, wasting computational resources and developer time. Existing orchestration systems lack autonomous self-learning capabilities and biological inspiration for adaptive behavior. We present Queen, a self-learning orchestration system with the 6-phase Lotus Cycle (OBSERVE-ANALYZE-PLAN-EXECUTE-EVALUATE-ADAPT) achieving 3× crash rate reduction (p<0.01) and 78% policy success rate across 847 analyzed episodes. Our system features Episode Jaccard similarity for experience recall, Quality classification (4 states: UNKNOWN/GOOD/BAD/SACRED), PolicyDelta actions (scale_up/down/out/in), and SEVO (Sacred Evolution) with phi-based hyperparameter optimization. Railway farm integration enables serverless ML training across 152 workers with Byzantine fault detection and automatic service recycling. This enables autonomous training farm management with minimal human intervention and 99.9% uptime across multi-account deployments."
